                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            partial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivatives
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            coincide.
          %p
            In the case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a trivial bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:X\times Y \to X
            its sections are canonically in bijection with maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and two sections have the same partial derivatives iff the partial derivatives of the corresponding maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            agree. So in this case the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+space"} jet space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi k
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^k P
            is called the space of jets of maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and commonly denoted with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^k(X,Y)
          %p
            In order to pass to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to \infty
            to form the
            %em infinite jet bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^\infty P
            one forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+limit"} projective limit
            over the finite-order jet bundles,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟵
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi k
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟵
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mn 3
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mn 1
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  J^\infty E \coloneqq \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_k J^k E
                  \=
                  \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}
                  \\left(
                  \\cdots J^3 E \to J^2 E \to J^1 E \to E
                  \\right)
          %p
            but one has to decide in which category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifolds"} infinite-dimensional manifolds
            to take this limit:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                one may form the limit formally, i.e. in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-manifolds"} pro-manifolds
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "#Anderson"} Anderson, p.3-5
            %li
              %p
                one may form the limit in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifolds"} Fréchet manifolds
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Saunders89"} Saunders 89, chapter 7
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "Frechet+manifold#ProjectiveLimitsOfSmoothFiniteDimensionalManifolds"} Fréchet manifold – Projective limits of finite-dimensional manifolds
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "Frechet+manifold#DifferenceBetweenProManifoldAndFrecherManifoldStructure"} here
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+pro-manifolds"} locally pro-manifolds
          %h3#the_atiyah_exact_sequence The Atiyah exact sequence
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{O}_X)
            is a complex-analytic manifold with the structure sheaf of holomorphic functions, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a locally free sheaf of
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^1(E)
            fits into a short exact sequence, called the Atiyah exact sequence:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0\to
                  E\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_X}\Omega_X^1\to
                  J^1(E)\to
                  E\to
                  0
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^1(E) = (E\otimes\Omega_X^1)\oplus E
            as a
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mi s
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ω
                  %mo +
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(s\otimes\omega,t)
                  \=
                  (f s\otimes\omega+t\otimes\mathrm{d}f, f t).
          %p
            The extension class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ext
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [J^1(E)]\in\mathrm{Ext}_{\mathcal{O}_X}^1(E,E\otimes\Omega_X^1)
            of this exact sequence is called the Atiyah class of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h3#GeneralAbstractDefinition General abstract
          %p
            We discuss a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            definition of jet bundles.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
            (or rather a tower
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im_k
            of such, for each infinitesimal order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}
            ).
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im(X)
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+space"} de Rham space
            object.
          %p
            Notice that we have the canonical morphism, the
            = succeed "-component" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \colon X \to \Im(X)
          %p (“inclusion of constant paths into all infinitesimal paths”).
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi Jet
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (i^\ast \dashv i_\ast)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/X}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{i^*}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{Jet := i_*}{\longrightarrow}}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\Im(X)}
          #GeneralAbstractDefinition.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-comonad"} (∞,1)-comonad
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i^\ast i_\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/X}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/X}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              gives even an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_! \dashv i^\ast \dashv i_\ast)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} X \times_X (-)
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
              of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAbstractDefinition"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Jet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T_{inf}X \times_X (-) \;\dashv\; Jet
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"} infinitesimal disk bundle
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohesion#RelationOfInfinitesimalDiskBundleToJetBundle"} differential cohesion – infinitesimal disk bundle – relation to jet bundles
          #LiteratureOnGeneralAbstractCharacterization.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              In the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              the fact that the jet bundle construction is a comonad was explicitly observed in (
              %a{:href => "#Marvan86"}> Marvan 86
              , see also
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Marvan93"} Marvan 93, section 1.1
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Marvan89"} Marvan 89
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#KrasilshchikVerbovetsky98"} Krasil’shchik-Verbovetsky 98, p. 13, p. 17
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Krasilshchik99"} Krasilshchik 99, p. 25
            %p
              In the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
              the fact that the jet bundle construction is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"} infinitesimal disk bundle
              construction is (
              %a{:href => "#Kock80"}> Kock 80, prop. 2.2
              ).
            %p#InTheContextOf
              In the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              and of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-schemes"} D-schemes
              as in (
              %a{:href => "#BeilinsonDrinfeld"}> BeilinsonDrinfeld, 2.3.2
              , reviewed in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Paugam"} Paugam, section 2.3
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAbstractDefinition"}
              was noticed in (
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 0.9
              ).
          %p
            In as in (
            %a{:href => "#BeilinsonDrinfeld"}> BeilinsonDrinfeld, 2.3.2
            , reviewed in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Paugam"} Paugam, section 2.3
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-modules"} D-modules
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              In terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+homotopy+type+theory"} differential homotopy type theory
              this means that forming “jet types” of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              operation along the unit of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi jet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℑ
                        %mi X
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    jet(E) \coloneqq \underset{X \to \Im X}{\prod} E
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} quasicoherent (∞,1)-sheaf
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-sheaves"} (∞,2)-sheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to Mod
                    \\,.
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC(X) := Hom(X, Mod)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} quasicoherent (∞,1)-sheaves
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} D-module
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-sheaves"} (∞,2)-sheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Im (X) \to Mod
                    \\,.
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DQC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DQC(X) := Hom(\Im (X), Mod)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
              of D-modules.
          %p
            The
            %strong Jet algebra
            functor is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} commutative algebras
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}(X)
            to those over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Jet
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Jet
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (Jet \dashv F)
                  \:
                  Alg_{\mathcal{D}(X)}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Jet}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{F}{\to}}
                  Alg_{\mathcal{O}(X)}
                  \\,.
