          %p
            Exposition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            in terms of jet bundles and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lepage+forms"} Lepage forms
            and aimed at examples from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is in
          %ul
            %li#MusilovaHronek16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jana+Musilov%C3%A1"}> Jana Musilová
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanislav+Hronek"} Stanislav Hronek
              = succeed "," do
                %em The calculus of variations on jet bundles as a universal approach for a variational formulation of fundamental physical theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/cm-2016-0012"} doi.org/10.1515/cm-2016-0012
          %p Lecture notes and textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Michor80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Michor"}> Peter Michor
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Jet Bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Manifolds of differentiable mappings
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~michor/manifolds_of_differentiable_mappings.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Saunders89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Saunders"}> David Saunders
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of jet bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 142
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511526411"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526411
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Demeter+Krupka"}> Demeter Krupka
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josef+Jany%C5%A1ka"} Josef Janyška
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on differential invariants
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/36792711_Lectures_on_Differential_Invariants"} researchgate
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois+Pommaret"}> Jean-François Pommaret
                , Chapter II in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Partial Differential Equations and Group Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-017-2539-2"} doi:10.1007/978-94-017-2539-2
            %li#Krasilshchik99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Krasil%27shchik"} Joseph Krasil'shchik
                in collaboration with Barbara Prinari,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Linear Differential Operators over Commutative Algebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://diffiety.mccme.ru/preprint/99/01_99.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Shihoko Ishii,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Jet schemes, arc spaces and the Nash problem
                %a{:href => "http://arXiv.org/abs/0704.3327"} arXiv:math.AG/0704.3327
            %li
              %p
                G. Sardanashvily,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibre bundles, jet manifolds and Lagrangian theory
                %a{:href => "http://xxx.lanl.gov/abs/0908.1886"} arXiv:0908.1886
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Olver"}> Peter Olver
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Lie groups and differential equation
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Jets and differential invariants
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.umn.edu/~olver/sm_/j.pdf"} pdf
          %p Early accounts include
          %ul
            %li
              Hubert Goldschmidt,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Integrability criteria for systems of nonlinear partial differential equations
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214428094"} Euclid
          %p
            The algebra of smooth functions of just
            %em locally
            finite order on the jet bundle (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+pro-manifold"}> locally pro-manifold
            ”) was maybe first considered in
          %ul
            %li#Takens79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Floris+Takens"}> Floris Takens
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A global version of the inverse problem of the calculus of variations
              %strong 14
              4 (1979) 543–562 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214435235"}> euclid:euclid.jdg/1214435235
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p#DiscussionOfFrechetManifoldStructure
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifold"} Fréchet manifold
            structure on infinite jet bundles includes
          %ul
            %li#Saunders89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Saunders"}> David Saunders
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Infinite jet bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of jet bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 142
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511526411"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526411
            %li
              %p
                M. Bauderon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential geometry and Lagrangian formalism in the calculus of variations
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry, Calculus of Variations, and their Applications
            %li#DodsonGalanisVassiliou15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+T.+J.+Dodson"}> C. T. J. Dodson
                , George Galanis, Efstathios Vassiliou,, p. 109 and section 6.3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry in a Fréchet Context: A Projective Limit Approach
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Lewis"}> Andrew Lewis
                ,
                %em The bundle of infinite jets
                (2006) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mast.queensu.ca/~andrew/notes/pdf/2006a.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Discussion of finite-order jet bundles in tems of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Kock80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formal manifolds and synthetic theory of jet bundles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1980__21_3_227_0"} Numdam
            %li#Kock10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                , section 2.7 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Synthetic geometry of manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/SGM-final.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
            structure on the jet operation in the context of differential geometry is made explicit in
          %ul
            %li#Marvan86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Marvan"}> Michal Marvan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A note on the category of partial differential equations
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential geometry and its applications
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MarvanJetComonad.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p (notice that prop. 1.3 there is wrong, the correct version is in the thesis of the author)
          %p with further developments in
          %ul
            %li#Marvan89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Marvan"} Michal Marvan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the horizontal cohomology with general coefficients
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://old.math.slu.cz/People/MichalMarvan/Annotations/horizontal.php"} web announcement
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dml.cz/dmlcz/701469"} web archive
              %p
                %strong Abstract:
                In the present paper the horizontal cohomology theory is interpreted as a special case of the Van Osdol bicohomology theory applied to what we call a “jet comonad”. It follows that differential equations have well-defined cohomology groups with coefficients in linear differential equations.
            %li#Marvan93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Marvan"}> Michal Marvan
                , section 1.1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Zero-Curvature Representations of Partial Differential Equations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.45.5631"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Synthetic+variational+calculus"} Synthetic geometry of differential equations: I. Jets and comonad structure
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06238"}> arXiv:1701.06238
                )
          %p In the context of algebraic geometry, the abstract characterization of jet bundles as the direct images of base change along the de Rham space projection is noticed in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , p. 6 of:
              %em
                Notes on crystals and algebraic
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lurie-NotesOnCrystals.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The explicit description in terms of formal duals of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} D-modules
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BeilinsonDrinfeld
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfeld"} Vladimir Drinfeld
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chiral+Algebras"} Chiral Algebras
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Paugam
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric+Paugam"}> Frédéric Paugam
              , Section 2.3 of:
              %em Homotopical Poisson Reduction of gauge theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~fpaugam/documents/homotopical-poisson-reduction-of-gauge-theories.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A discussion of jet bundles with an eye towards discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
            on them :
          %ul
            %li#Anderson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Anderson"}> Ian Anderson
              , chapter 1, section A of:
              %em The variational bicomplex
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/AndersonVariationalBicomplex.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
            of jet bundles is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              G. Giachetta, L. Mangiarotti,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennadi+Sardanashvily"} Gennadi Sardanashvily
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cohomology of the variational bicomplex on the infinite order jet space
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0006074"} arXiv:math/0006074
          %p where both versions (smooth functions being globally or locally of finite order) are discussed and compared.
          %p
            Discussion of all this in the convenient context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
          %ul
            %li#GiotopoulosSati23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigorios+Giotopoulos"}> Grigorios Giotopoulos
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %em
                Field Theory via Higher Geometry I:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Smooth+Sets+of+Fields"} Smooth Sets of Fields
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.16301"}> arXiv:2312.16301
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion of jet-restriction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haefliger+groupoid"} Haefliger groupoid
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Arne Lorenz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Jet Groupoids, Natural Bundles and the Vessiot Equivalence Method
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://wwwb.math.rwth-aachen.de/~arne/Dissertation_Lorenz_Arne.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of jet bundles in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Arthemy V. Kiselev, Andrey O. Krutov, appendix of
                %em
                  On the (non)removability of spectral parameters in
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.7143"}> arXiv:1301.7143
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennadi+Sardanashvily"}> Gennadi Sardanashvily
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Graded infinite order jet manifolds
                %em Int. J. Geom. Methods Mod. Phys. v.4 (2007) 1335-1362
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2434"}> arXiv:0708.2434
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#KrasilshchikVerbovetsky98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Krasil%27shchik"}> Joseph Krasil'shchik
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Verbovetsky"} Alexander Verbovetsky
              %em Homological Methods in Equations of Mathematical Physics
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9808130"}> arXiv:math/9808130
              )
          %p
            On jet bundles of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+manifold"} graded manifolds
            and their
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Vysoky"}> Jan Vysoky
              \.
              = succeed "." do
                %em Graded Jet Geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.15754"} arXiv:2311.15754
          %p
            On jet bundles in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shahn+Majid"}> Shahn Majid
                , Francisco Simão,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum jet bundles
                %strong 113
                120 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03067"}> arXiv:2202.03067
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-023-01738-z"} doi:10.1007/s11005-023-01738-z
            %li
              %p
                Xiao Han,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shahn+Majid"} Shahn Majid
                %em Quantum jet Hopf algebroids by cotwist
                (2025). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.02848"}> arXiv:2507.02848
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Jet functors in noncommutative geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00029-025-01064-3"} doi.org/10.1007/s00029-025-01064-3
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
                %em Symbols in noncommutative geometry
                (2023). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.00835"}> arXiv:2308.00835
                )
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
                %em Higher order connections in noncommutative geometry
                (2025). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.05519"}> arXiv:2504.05519
                )
        .revisedby
          %p
